{"uid":"9f539e4b785dae3b","name":"test_bounded_tail_is_byte_identical_to_full_render_across_a_many_delta_thinking_block","fullName":"tests.test_log_render_bounded_tail#test_bounded_tail_is_byte_identical_to_full_render_across_a_many_delta_thinking_block","historyId":"0a6f382fd466fda367960800f6232694","time":{"start":1791956865823,"stop":1791956865839,"duration":16},"description":"Task 044 (PRD H.2): the bounded-tail path (`render_tail_lines`) and\n    the previous full-render path (`render_to_lines`, unchanged by task\n    043) must render the SAME bytes for the same tail -- not merely the\n    same line count -- once a many-delta thinking block sits inside the\n    requested window. The flood lands in the NEWEST iteration so a\n    10-line tail (iterations 6-8) spans it, forcing the bounded path's\n    chunk-grown window to restart at the boundary immediately before the\n    flood and re-render it from a fresh `new_render_state()`, exactly as\n    the full render's single pass would have.","descriptionHtml":"<p>Task 044 (PRD H.2): the bounded-tail path (<code>render_tail_lines</code>) and<br />\nthe previous full-render path (<code>render_to_lines</code>, unchanged by task<br />\n043) must render the SAME bytes for the same tail -- not merely the<br />\nsame line count -- once a many-delta thinking block sits inside the<br />\nrequested window. The flood lands in the NEWEST iteration so a<br />\n10-line tail (iterations 6-8) spans it, forcing the bounded path's<br />\nchunk-grown window to restart at the boundary immediately before the<br />\nflood and re-render it from a fresh <code>new_render_state()</code>, exactly as<br />\nthe full render's single pass would have.</p>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791956453364,"stop":1791956453364,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"paramet